        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "I really like how `mini.hues` basically follows 2 stages:\r\n\r\n1. create a color palette from high level parameters (_hue, saturation, accent..._)\r\n2. apply that palette to create consistent highlight groups\r\n\r\nThe 1st stage already is exposed, through `MiniHues.make_palette`.  \r\nThe 2nd one isn't: @echasnovski, could you consider exposing it also, with a `MiniHues.apply_palette` function for instance ?\r\n",
